rs down your spine whether Paul  Dano is the Riddler and Colin Farrell as  the penguin will find their way back  into the story is still unknown but the  latter will get his own series anyway  the movie is expected to be released in  2024 a more specific date has  unfortunately not been announced yet  a reboot has finally made it back into  the MCU although most of you may not  have known that it was based on a Marvel  movie we're talking about the Vampire  Hunter blade from the 1998 film of the  same name who was played by Wesley  Snipes at the time and goes out hunting  vampires at night however he himself is  a half vampire as his mother was bitten  by a vampire during her pregnancy since  he was born he is also known as  daywalker he has the same power as the  nocturnal creatures yet the sun doesn't  bother him and garlic and silver don't  seem to weaken him either in the new  part he'll be played by mahershala Ali  who was last seen in Swanson kit  Harrington is also likely to make his  second appearance in the MCU he was  introduced to the MCU in eternals and  will finally take on the role of the  Black Knight how the Vampire Hunter will  fit into the MCU remains to be seen as  his first movies were mainly dark and  gory which is nothing you would  recognize from past movies the  provisional release date so far is  September 6 2024 but a lot can still  change in the meantime  this was the first part of our superhero  preview of the next few years which  movie are you most looking forward to so  far let us know in the comments and if  you like this video feel free to leave a  thumbs up  [Music]

